# Netlify response headers (publish dir is docs/, so this file is picked up on deploy).
#
# The staff console must never load inside another site's frame: a page that
# framed it invisibly could trick a logged-in member of staff into clicking
# Annulla or Elimina (clickjacking). Header-only and frame-ancestors only — a
# full script CSP broke admin.html once, so this deliberately restricts nothing
# else. Both paths, because Netlify also serves the page at /admin.
/admin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
/admin.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
